From eb01f9b3010fe44e4e97ffdfb8142b30f220da2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zswll2 <zswll2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:46:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/32] feat(desktop): iOS/touch adaptations for the web build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

viewport-fit=cover plus safe-area CSS vars; the composer's rich input sits at
max(1rem, 16px) so iOS Safari never focus-zooms the viewport; the chat surface
contains overscroll and buttons drop the double-tap-zoom delay via
touch-action: manipulation. useVisualViewportInset mirrors the keyboard's
occluded height into --keyboard-inset (iOS never resizes window.innerHeight)
and the composer dock pads against it. The narrow-viewport pane overlay gains
a backdrop + slide-in for PINNED reveals — the toggle-driven drawer touch
needs, with an obvious tap-anywhere dismissal — while hover reveals keep
their weightless behavior; desktop is unaffected (env() insets are 0,
visualViewport matches the window).
